      { name: "Confirm the symptoms are a worn cylinder", text: "A chair that slowly sinks under your weight, will not stay at the set height, or feels bouncy when you sit is showing gas cylinder wear. The cylinder is a sealed pressurized tube and cannot be repaired — only replaced." },
      { name: "Measure Class 3 versus Class 4 cylinder", text: "Office chair cylinders come in Class 3 (rated for up to 250 lbs) and Class 4 (rated for 250-400 lbs). Class 4 cylinders have thicker walls and higher pressure. Measure the current cylinder or check the chair's weight rating." },
      { name: "Confirm the universal 2-inch top diameter", text: "Most office chairs use a standard 2-inch (50mm) top taper and 2-inch bottom taper. Measure the top where it enters the seat mechanism to verify before buying a replacement kit." },
